#: ../../technical/articles/071-calculation-findings-reports-and-pdf-verification.md:10
msgid "Scope"
msgstr "Ámbito"

#: ../../technical/articles/071-calculation-findings-reports-and-pdf-verification.md:12
msgid ""
"This chunk covers 18 calculation application files (5,071 lines; 220,527 "
"bytes; 46,042 `o200k_base` proxy tokens): calculation note gating and "
"storage, public calculation projection, persistence binding, report "
"models and serialization, export, provenance-key derivation, "
"document/store verification, request fields, channel resolution, and "
"route policy. I read every assigned file in bounded sections; no ranges "
"remain unread. This is static inspection only. No application or tests "
"were run, and the PDF adapter, repository implementations, and UI "
"consumers are outside the chunk."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/071-calculation-findings-reports-and-pdf-verification.md:14
msgid "Capabilities and mechanisms"
msgstr "Capacidades y mecanismos"

#: ../../technical/articles/071-calculation-findings-reports-and-pdf-verification.md:16
msgid ""
"The typed request model accepts bounded, unique casilla, binding, and "
"relation override lists and validates shortcut amounts using canonical "
"finite-decimal grammar before delegating to the shared bundle builder "
"(request fields "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/modelo/calculation_request_fields.py`)). "
"Channel resolution overlays profile, backend, borrador, and caller "
"binding values in that order, retaining decimal, enum, date, and boolean "
"channels separately. Casilla inputs merge declaration-period facts, "
"backend values, bound values, then caller overrides; text inputs have a "
"parallel merge. Replay payloads serialize the values the engine actually "
"consumed into canonical strings, including structured row indexes "
"(binding resolution "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/modelo/calculation_resolution.py`), casilla "
"merge (`src/cadrumo/application/modelo/calculation_resolution.py`), "
"replay payload "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/modelo/calculation_resolution.py`))."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/071-calculation-findings-reports-and-pdf-verification.md:18
msgid ""
"The route table lists pre-mesh, mesh, conditional, post-mesh, manual, and"
" design-constant ownership. Import-time checks require every executable "
"resolver exactly once, unique IDs, matching source registrations/stages, "
"and no unregistered runtime source beyond two named mesh-only kinds. The "
"runtime resolver check also confirms stage, ID, and source ownership "
"against the table (route ownership "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/modelo/calculation_route.py`), registration "
"agreement (`src/cadrumo/application/modelo/calculation_route.py`), "
"runtime check (`src/cadrumo/application/modelo/calculation_route.py`)). "
"Source lock and carry sets are projected from the aggregation precedence "
"ladder rather than separately enumerated (source policy "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/modelo/calculation_source_policy.py`)). The "
"publication value object binds a revision to the parent work unit and "
"distinguishes a newly published write from a duplicate result; the "
"repository factory must be explicitly bound in context and has no "
"implicit fallback (publication "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/modelo/calculation_publication.py`), repository"
" binding (`src/cadrumo/application/modelo/calculation_repository.py`))."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/071-calculation-findings-reports-and-pdf-verification.md:20
msgid ""
"Persisted calculation notes have a closed reason taxonomy. Gate-refused "
"reasons block checking, export, and recording; other blocking reasons are"
" handled by check or export steps. An unrouted OSS observation is "
"specifically left to Modelo 369’s own check. The gate uses the catalogue "
"sentence for the first blocking reason and includes all reason codes in "
"the refusal context (reason sets "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/modelo/calculation_notes.py`), gate "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/modelo/calculation_note_gate.py`)). A startup "
"invariant compares the attention map to every diagnostic reason and "
"ensures its blocking level exactly matches the combined refusal sets "
"(level invariant "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/modelo/calculation_notes.py`)). Nonblocking "
"diagnostics are held only in a lock-protected process-local store and "
"disappear when the process closes; only selected blocking source issues "
"persist on the revision (note store "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/modelo/calculation_notes.py`))."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/071-calculation-findings-reports-and-pdf-verification.md:22
msgid ""
"A calculation report is a typed snapshot of a sealed revision with header"
" coordinates, verification/filing references, taxpayer identity, registry"
" generation, optional ledger fingerprint, and one registry-ordered row "
"per casilla. Rows preserve input/computed/subtotal/result roles and "
"distinguish value, absent, and not-applicable states. Canonical JSON "
"bytes have a content version and their SHA-256 is derived over those "
"exact bytes (report model "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/modelo/calculation_report.py`), canonical "
"digest (`src/cadrumo/application/modelo/calculation_report.py`), builder "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/modelo/calculation_report.py`)). The CSV uses "
"fixed columns and commented header metadata, with the product’s shared "
"tabular serializer. The PDF port receives the exact report and CSV bytes "
"and a callback that signs only after the writer has finalized the visible"
" page layer (CSV serializer "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/modelo/calculation_report_document.py`), PDF "
"serializer "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/modelo/calculation_report_document.py`), PDF "
"ports "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/modelo/calculation_summary_pdf_ports.py`))."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/071-calculation-findings-reports-and-pdf-verification.md:24
msgid ""
"The export action requires an exportable sealed revision, resolves the "
"filer’s identity and current filing/verification facts, and writes CSV or"
" PDF to the requested local path through the shared export sink. Existing"
" files require the explicit `replace_existing` choice. PDF export checks "
"the optional dependency and requires a supplied writer before profile "
"reads. The receipt includes byte and report digests but omits taxpayer "
"identity (export command/result "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/modelo/calculation_report_export.py`), report "
"assembly (`src/cadrumo/application/modelo/calculation_report_export.py`),"
" export (`src/cadrumo/application/modelo/calculation_report_export.py`))."
" The artifact intentionally shows the taxpayer’s full name and tax "
"identifier and states that it is a local calculation, not AEAT evidence."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/071-calculation-findings-reports-and-pdf-verification.md:26
msgid ""
"Third-party source references are protected in the report with a per-"
"profile HMAC key derived in memory from the existing Ed25519 review-"
"package key under a separate label. Recognized lowercase source-family "
"names remain visible, while the whole reference is digested; canonical "
"SHA-256 source-content fingerprints are carried as SHA-256, other forms "
"are keyed. The raw secret uses `SecretBytes` and is not persisted "
"(provenance key "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/modelo/calculation_report_provenance_key.py`), "
"derivation "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/modelo/calculation_report_provenance_key.py`), "
"report provenance projection "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/modelo/calculation_report.py`)). PDF "
"certification signs a domain-separated digest of a canonical statement "
"binding report, CSV, visible-page digests, revision and authority "
"coordinates, export time, and public-key fingerprint. `aeat_official` is "
"fixed to false. The signature does not assert tax correctness, source "
"truth, taxpayer consent, trusted time, or AEAT acceptance (statement "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/modelo/calculation_report_certification.py`), "
"signing "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/modelo/calculation_report_certification.py`))."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/071-calculation-findings-reports-and-pdf-verification.md:28
msgid ""
"Verification has a document layer and optional store layer. The document "
"layer checks PDF readability, required attachments, canonical "
"statement/report JSON, signature, report and CSV digests, metadata, page-"
"layer digest/overlays, report-to-statement coordinates, CSV derivation, "
"and whether extracted page text shows the report’s figures and identity "
"(document checks "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/modelo/calculation_report_verification.py`)). "
"Without a trusted key or store, a consistent document is "
"`valid_unpinned`; a self-signer cannot turn that into `verified`. With a "
"store, the verifier pins the key to the active profile, resolves the "
"named revision, checks work-unit, registry, verification and filing "
"facts, requires matching authority generation, rebuilds the report at the"
" original export time, and compares provenance and digest. Later "
"filing/state changes are reported separately (store trace "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/modelo/calculation_report_verification.py`), "
"verifier entrypoint "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/modelo/calculation_report_verification.py`)). A"
" registered operation binds the request to a profile, absolute path, and "
"source digest; it reads and hashes the bytes before constructing exact-"
"profile ports, applies the whole-profile tax-value access capability, and"
" stores the bounded result through secure references (operation "
"request/executor "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/modelo/calculation_report_verification_operation.py`),"
" definition "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/modelo/calculation_report_verification_operation.py`),"
" access registration "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/modelo/calculation_report_verification_operation.py`))."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/071-calculation-findings-reports-and-pdf-verification.md:30
msgid "Security and implementation assessment"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/071-calculation-findings-reports-and-pdf-verification.md:32
msgid ""
"The strongest controls here are canonical content hashing, Ed25519 domain"
" separation, profile-key pinning, explicit `valid_unpinned` semantics, "
"dual-layer verification, and keyed redaction of third-party source "
"references. Reports deliberately include the filer’s own full identity, "
"so the local file is sensitive even though the machine-readable receipt "
"is not. The per-profile HMAC also makes the same source reference "
"linkable across that profile’s reports, which appears useful for "
"provenance continuity. A public calculation projection also carries raw "
"`source_ref` values in its `ModeloCalculationSourceSnapshot`; its "
"caller/access boundary is outside this chunk, so confirm that projection "
"is kept within the intended profile boundary (projection source trace "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/modelo/calculation_projection.py`), snapshot "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/modelo/calculation_projection.py`))."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/071-calculation-findings-reports-and-pdf-verification.md:34
msgid ""
"One conditional state-classification risk needs an upstream invariant: "
"`_row_value_state` tests `realised_kind == EMPTY` before "
"`absent_by_design`. If the review-row producer permits both facts at "
"once, the report will call the row `ABSENT` instead of `NOT_APPLICABLE`; "
"this chunk does not establish whether that combination is possible (state"
" classifier (`src/cadrumo/application/modelo/calculation_report.py`)). "
"Also, document verification depends on the injected PDF reader correctly "
"extracting all overlays and computing the page-layer digest; this chunk "
"defines the contract and checks returned facts but does not inspect the "
"concrete PDF parser/writer. The optional trusted public key is meaningful"
" only if the caller obtained it out of band; otherwise document-only "
"verification correctly remains unpinned."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/071-calculation-findings-reports-and-pdf-verification.md:36
msgid ""
"The repository contains structural checks in code (route tables and "
"strict models), but this chunk contains no tests or runtime evidence. "
"Follow-up should inspect the PDF adapters, the capability that stores "
"signing keys, the local-file sink, export-state rules, and access "
"controls on calculation projections. Cross-check the report-state "
"combination with work-review row construction and confirm each durable "
"note is consumed by the correct check/export gate."
msgstr ""

